       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg, and a typical starting dose is 2.5\u20135 mg. At 50 mg the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or prolonged vasodilatory shock. Overdoses in that range have caused serious harm, and the drug's long half-life means effects can last for days.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (standard starting dose)\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (maximum dose)\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily (for a frail patient or one with a low blood pressure margin)\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intend, for example as part of an unusual protocol, please tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
